{
  "about": "Settings' Displays from the keyboard with the screen reader on in Spanish (docs/adr/0039-keyboard-access.mdx), as a Mac's Displays settings with Full Keyboard Access and VoiceOver, on two displays as a card reports them (a 14-inch panel, the main one, and a 24-inch monitor right of it). The arrangement's displays are keyboard stops said with where they stand ('OxyOS Monitor, right of Built-in Display') and the arrows' hint; the arrows move the focused display to that side of the other, each move said once by its new place, a move to where it already is going nowhere, saying nothing; Space chooses it. A resolution chosen from the keyboard is on trial: its dialog takes the keyboard on Revert, its default button, and is said by its title, its countdown and Revert; Escape reverts, Return reverts, and the keyboard goes back to Resolution each time; left alone it says its countdown at 10 and 5 seconds, not each second, and that the display went back; Keep Changes is a Tab away and keeps it. The settings' Saved toast is never in the tree while unseen. Every step checks the keyboard's focus, what the assistive technology holds, what the reader says and what is announced. At 1 (the panel at 1, 1920 × 1200, as chosen before).",
